      "math_academy_id": "q-84008",
      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "If $\\text{E}[X]=8$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=71,$ then what is $\\text{Var}[X]?$",
      "worked_solution": "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =71-{8}^{2} \\\\  & =71-64 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
